.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Version 1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple Unix command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple Unix command language interpreter that executes commands read from standard input or from a file.

.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 4
Displays a prompt and waits for the user to type a command.
.IP \(bu 4
Executes executable files located in the directories listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable, as well as absolute and relative paths.
.IP \(bu 4
Handles command lines with arguments separated by spaces or tabs.
.IP \(bu 4
Supports interactive and non-interactive modes.
.IP \(bu 4
Implements built-in commands
.B exit
and
.B env
\&.

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell with the status code of the last executed command.
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables to standard output.

.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.SS Interactive Mode
Start the shell:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ ./hsh
/your/current/directory$ ls -l
/your/current/directory$ pwd
/your/current/directory$ exit
.fi
.RE

.SS Non-Interactive Mode
Pipe commands into the shell:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
$ echo "ls -l" | ./hsh
$ echo "env" | ./hsh
.fi
.RE

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the status of the last executed command, or 127 if a command was not found.

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If a command is not found, the shell prints an error message to standard error formatted as:
.PP
.RS 4
\fIprog_name\fR: \fIline_number\fR: \fIcommand\fR: not found
.RE

